{"id": "EUVD-2026-103931", "enisaUuid": "f925a212-fc44-3cdb-b3e3-e07d41cca2c9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: adc: ad_sigma_delta: fix use-after-free on unbind\n\nad_sd_buffer_postenable() allocates sigma_delta->samples_buf with\ndevm_krealloc() at runtime, so its devres entry sits after all\nprobe-time entries of the driver. devm resources are released in\nreverse allocation order, which means unbind frees samples_buf before\niio_device_unregister() disables the buffers and detaches the trigger\npollfunc. The data ready IRQ is still enabled at that point, so\nad_sd_trigger_handler() can still run and memcpy() incoming samples\ninto the freed samples_buf.\n\nFix this by preallocating the buffer in\ndevm_ad_sd_setup_buffer_and_trigger(), before the triggered buffer and\nthe IRQ are set up, so it is freed only after iio_device_unregister()\nhas drained the trigger handler via free_irq(). Size it for the worst\ncase of all sequencer slots being active; ad_sd_validate_scan_mask()\nalready caps the number of active channels at num_slots.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:45:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:38", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/975b09bc680acc60903777b766cdb53b0bf9c9f6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/84500ae0d976995a6870cb1dca2d124b6b2d6e5a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f20b94a7dc1ff9ade191ce839c984210fdbdc653", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5663c72bf400231e90777982216797191887a6b9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9ee8306121495d2a25aa5d1bfd519f2748786b83"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98677", "GHSA-852j-fqfh-mmqj"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "43cc0eaf-500a-3125-b19d-df0f7e1092f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "4bb0c0c0-dc9c-3956-a0a9-077c35dcb4e4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "74b2f849-11f6-3316-97fa-0efcaaf40b73", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8bea9af887de4c99a95f93f2ce400ef63e8b4e9b <9ee8306121495d2a25aa5d1bfd519f2748786b83"}, {"id": "7572e462-567a-390d-abc1-437d8f659923", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8bea9af887de4c99a95f93f2ce400ef63e8b4e9b <975b09bc680acc60903777b766cdb53b0bf9c9f6"}, {"id": "798b9218-267b-3c00-a350-63d8a4397f2d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "a2e4b1b0-7d83-3e29-8baf-039d905aa652", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "add6c2f3-98a7-3b41-bfb0-6c67d138d058", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "b62ae813-e8ab-3d8b-9175-b56cbb1b3f02", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8bea9af887de4c99a95f93f2ce400ef63e8b4e9b <f20b94a7dc1ff9ade191ce839c984210fdbdc653"}, {"id": "bbc9b853-0119-3a86-ab86-393d16d7a5bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.19"}, {"id": "dc93f636-ad07-3571-86d7-8cd0e795bc69", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8bea9af887de4c99a95f93f2ce400ef63e8b4e9b <5663c72bf400231e90777982216797191887a6b9"}, {"id": "ed24490e-6185-3327-a0ce-61fde8e89106", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8bea9af887de4c99a95f93f2ce400ef63e8b4e9b <84500ae0d976995a6870cb1dca2d124b6b2d6e5a"}, {"id": "eee21976-97a0-38fc-bd24-6b645c06bcee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1ec5e1f7-6c3f-3d4b-9c98-9e0084639536", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}